\title{zzlongplot: Longitudinal Plotting with Clinical Trials Support}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Provides a formula interface for defining longitudinal plots with optional grouping, change-from-baseline panels, and faceting. Includes specialized support for clinical trials with CDISC variable detection, regulatory and journal themes, and publication-ready export.
}
\details{
The core workflow is a single call to \code{\link[=lplot]{lplot()}}, which parses a
formula, computes summary statistics, and renders the plot:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=lplot]{lplot()}}: the main entry point. Produces the observed plot, the
change-from-baseline plot, or both combined.
\item \code{\link[=parse_formula]{parse_formula()}}: extracts response, time, grouping, and faceting
variables from a \code{y ~ x | group} formula.
\item \code{\link[=compute_stats]{compute_stats()}}: computes the per-timepoint summary statistics
that drive the plot, optionally with hypothesis tests.
\item \code{\link[=generate_plot]{generate_plot()}}: renders a statistics data frame as a ggplot.
}

Clinical trial support is provided by \code{\link[=suggest_clinical_vars]{suggest_clinical_vars()}},
\code{\link[=validate_cdisc_data]{validate_cdisc_data()}}, and \code{\link[=get_cdisc_template]{get_cdisc_template()}}. Journal and
regulatory styling is provided by \code{\link[=get_publication_theme]{get_publication_theme()}} and the
\verb{theme_*()} family. Export helpers are \code{\link[=publication_panels]{publication_panels()}} and
\code{\link[=save_publication]{save_publication()}}.
}
